Sval: Nimbus does not report its shutdown rejection when nothing awaits it

SharedDataMap rejects its readiness promise when the app shuts down before
the store loads, to release whoever awaits ready(). When nothing does, the
rejection is reported as an uncaught "SharedDataMap: in shutdown" error, as
on quitting seconds after a fresh profile's first start.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/SharedDataMap.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/SharedDataMap.sys.mjs
index 6e4c1c10c3..fd4863db45 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/SharedDataMap.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/SharedDataMap.sys.mjs
@@ -21,6 +21,9 @@ export class SharedDataMap extends EventEmitter {
     this._sharedDataKey = sharedDataKey;
     this._isReady = false;
     this._readyDeferred = Promise.withResolvers();
+    // A shutdown rejects this only to release whoever awaits ready(), so it is
+    // not an error when nobody does.
+    this._readyDeferred.promise.catch(() => {});
     this._data = null;
     this._db = null;
 
